{"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"What the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types do that their signatures do not say.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SynapsesSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Working with the models"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/WorkingWithModels"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/Positioning","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/Maps","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/LiveData","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/BlueGPS","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/APIError","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/EnvironmentModel"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Most model types in this SDK are plain data: they mirror the JSON the backend sends, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reading the properties is enough to know what you get. A handful of behaviours, though,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are not visible in the declarations and will bite if you assume otherwise. They are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"listed here once rather than repeated on every type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Default values do not survive decoding","level":2,"anchor":"Default-values-do-not-survive-decoding","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A property written like this looks like it defaults to ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public var required: Bool? = false"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It does — but only when you construct the value in Swift. The synthesized ","type":"text"},{"code":"Decodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"decodeIfPresent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so when the key is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"absent from the JSON the property decodes to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not to the default"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are then two different states you have to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tell apart yourself.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Treat every ","type":"text"},{"code":"T? = someDefault","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a decoded model as “may be ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whatever the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"suggests”, and write the fallback at the point of use:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["if element.required ?? false { … }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The properties this applies to carry a note saying so.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`id` is local, not the backend’s identifier","level":2,"anchor":"id-is-local-not-the-backends-identifier","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Several models are ","type":"text"},{"code":"Identifiable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" through a property declared like this:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public var id = UUID()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That property is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" in the type’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"CodingKeys","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it is never decoded: a fresh UUID","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is minted every time an instance is created, decoding included. Two decodes of the very","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same JSON therefore carry different ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This matters more than it looks, because ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" include ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comparing two instances decoded from identical payloads returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and they land in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"different buckets of a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Set"},{"text":" or a dictionary. Use it as SwiftUI identity within one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"render pass — that is what it is for — and compare backend identity through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"backend’s own field ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/TicketComment\/commentId","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", a resource’s own id, and so on)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Watch for the related remap: in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/TicketComment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" the JSON field "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" decodes into","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/TicketComment\/commentId","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", precisely because ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is taken.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Timestamps are milliseconds","level":2,"anchor":"Timestamps-are-milliseconds","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Backend timestamps arrive as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"milliseconds","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" since the epoch, not seconds —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/BGPGPSPosition\/positionTS","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/TicketComment\/creationTimestamp","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and their siblings."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Passing one straight to "},{"code":"Date(timeIntervalSince1970:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a date tens of thousands of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"years in the future. Divide by 1000, or use the convenience the model already offers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/TicketComment\/creationDate","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The exceptions announce themselves in the name: fields ending in "},{"code":"Second","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/BGPSPositionCoordinator\/lastPositionNotOlderThan(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"code":"seconds","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter is in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fact compared against a millisecond difference."}]},{"anchor":"Unknown-enum-values-decode-they-do-not-throw","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Unknown enum values decode, they do not throw"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Enums conforming to "},{"code":"SafeCodableEnums","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" map any value this SDK version does not recognise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"onto their last case — "},{"code":"UNKNOWN","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":"unknown","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A backend that adds a new status will not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"break decoding, so a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"text":" over one of these enums must handle that case rather than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assume the set is closed. Never send ","type":"text"},{"code":"UNKNOWN","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" back: it is an inbound fallback, not a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value the backend accepts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some collections offer a "},{"code":"filterUnknownValues","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" flag to drop those entries instead of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"handing them to you.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Memberwise-initialisers-are-internal","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Memberwise initialisers are internal"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Model structs get the compiler’s membe